# dsv41: the DeepSeek-V4.1 prefill's DAX window, against upstream dfa3f402 (v0.2.4.2, engine 0.1.49.2).
#
# The dsv41 engine's prefill is its own flow (src/dsv41/ds4_model.cu: flow_push / flow_spec / flow_pump), not the
# Qwen engine's ExpertSource/Prefill, so tiberius.patch's STRATA_REGISTER_DAX window does not reach it.  Today every
# streamed expert is O_DIRECT pread into pinned staging and then copied to VRAM: one read stream at 0.5-1.0 GB/s from
# the fsdax /optane mount, with the 2080 Ti waiting 19-32 s per prompt.
#
# This patch adds the window to the flow, in that one file:
#   * DaxWin: the page-rounded span of a layer's expert blocks that touch in one shard file - the GGUF holds w1, w3
#     and w2 of every expert of a layer side by side (tensors.txt: layer 0 = 2.654 GB, layer 39 = 2.937 GB, the pack's
#     largest 3.327 GB), so one window a layer here - registered cudaHostRegisterReadOnly|Mapped|Portable.  The driver
#     caps a process's registered host memory at
#     ~7 GiB (8192 MiB is refused with cudaErrorOutOfMemory, 6912 MiB is the documented-good single allocation), and
#     a layer's experts are 2.65-3.33 GB, so the budget holds exactly two layer windows and the rotation is
#     double-buffered: the previous window is released only when a third must be registered.  With a budget below
#     twice the largest layer's span, every second layer reads from the files instead (logged once) - never a release
#     of a window whose copies may still be queued.
#   * dax_prepare(il) at the top of flow_spec, the prompt path's issue step (the initial call in run_dev_chunks and
#     every subsequent (chunk, layer) pass through it).  Never from decode: a decode visits 40 layers a token.
#     cudaStreamSynchronize runs on a release only - nothing may read a window after cudaHostUnregister, and the
#     driver does not defend a use-after-unmap.  cudaGetLastError() consumes a refused registration (sticky error).
#   * flow_push takes each matrix's address from pk.maps[file] + Layer::mx_off/mx_stride and, when the WHOLE item
#     (all three matrices) is inside a registered window, sets src[] plus stage = -1 (the flow's existing "no read
#     job, no staging slot" sentinel) and left = 0: flow_pump's read-job branch is skipped and its DMA copies
#     straight out of the mapping.  All-or-nothing per item: a partly covered blob would be an H2D from pageable
#     memory (2.3 GB/s) or a fault.
#   * it_dax counts those items in the prompt stream's report (and its GB/s denominator) and in the flow-vs-windows
#     picker, so the direct bytes are not read as a regression.
#
# Off by default: STRATA_REGISTER_DAX=1 (or DS4_REGISTER_DAX=1) turns it on, STRATA_REGISTER_DAX_MIB /
# DS4_REGISTER_DAX_MIB sets the budget (default 6912).  Refused with a log line when the prompt path is not the flow,
# when there is more than one GPU or tensor parallel is not 1, when DS4_STORE_ZC is on (the store's arena registers
# from the same cap), or when the pack is not a GGUF read in place.  Engram stays unregistered (it lives on /data, not
# DAX) and the drafter's mtp blocks are not windows.  Windows are unregistered in ~Impl, before Pack's mappings are
# unmapped.
#
# Expect "ds4: DAX window: 6912 MiB budget, N layer windows ..." at load, then a prompt stream line whose "from the
# DAX window" count is nearly every expert streamed and whose GB/s is ~6 instead of ~1.
#
# Anchor points (pin dfa3f402): Pack::map/at, Layer::mx_file/mx_off/mx_stride (expert_layout_mx), Chunk::Item and its
# counters, flow_push/flow_spec/flow_pump, the flow setup in load(), the prompt stream report and the picker, and
# ~Impl's teardown.  Regenerate against any new pin; `patch -p1`/`git apply` must apply cleanly or the build fails.

